WEBVTT

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:09.070
The attack on Asakura must have shown you 
what kind of man Nobunaga is.

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:12.810
He destroys anyone who opposes him.

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:17.580
He may one day point 
his sword at Azai.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:19.550
Is that not true?

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:22.580
Answer, Nagamasa!

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:29.340
Beginning today, our enemy is

00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:35.190
Nobunaga Oda!

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:46.020
<b>Episode 8</b>

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:46.020
<b>An Unthinkable Betrayal</b>

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:49.020
Chacha!

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:51.720
Chacha!

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:55.900
There you are!

00:00:57.270 --> 00:01:00.120
Chacha, wake up.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.030
Chacha!

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:08.890
What a weird face.

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:12.020
I am impressed by the lord's resolve.

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:18.440
Azai's reputation will echo far and wide 
if we defeat Oda and take Nobunaga's head.

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:22.240
Nobunaga became famous for 
killing Yoshimoto Imagawa,

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:25.250
and now Azai will kill Nobunaga 
and become famous!

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:26.140
Yeah.

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:30.160
I'm sure we can take him 
if we surround him.

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:33.730
We'll have him like a bagged rat.

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:37.340
Brother? Like a bagged rat?

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:41.360
What are those men talking about?

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:45.960
Asakura's forces didn't resist 
as much as we thought they would.

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:50.380
I expected it to take longer 
to take their castle.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:55.940
Their armor looked 
pretty heavy, didn't it?

00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:57.390
True.

00:01:57.390 --> 00:02:02.410
Their armor was somewhat more 
old-fashioned than ours.

00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:05.690
They ought to get rid of 
some of that weight.

00:02:05.690 --> 00:02:08.160
Then they could 
move around more easily.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:13.190
My lord, if the enemy became more mobile,
they would be harder to fight.

00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:15.400
Oh. Oh, yeah.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:19.910
My lord, we're attacking 
Kanegasaki Castle tomorrow, aren't we?

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:20.930
Yeah.

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:25.700
But honestly, I wish they'd 
just surrender.

00:02:27.070 --> 00:02:31.000
It should've been obvious from our battle today 
how much bigger our forces are.

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:34.900
I'm sure Asakura knows that, too.

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:39.210
So I'll probably send a messenger 
to encourage them to surrender.

00:02:39.210 --> 00:02:41.390
I believe that is the 
best course of action.

00:02:41.710 --> 00:02:45.600
If we take Kanegasaki Castle,
we can go down Kinome Pass,

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:50.430
and storm into Asakura 
headquarters in Ichijodani.

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:53.310
We are on the verge 
of defeating Asakura.

00:02:55.930 --> 00:02:56.860
Yep.

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:10.930
Oichi.

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:14.340
Where are you going?

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:20.770
I intended to let you know first, 
but things are quite hectic.

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:28.350
I'm on my way to support 
Nobunaga-dono's army.

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:29.920
Support?

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:35.930
Are you not going to pray for my success?

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:39.570
I always do, Nagamasa-dono.

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:42.280
For my brother.

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:49.130
I'll be leaving.

00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:59.150
Do not fear Oda's massive army!

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:02.830
All we need is Nobunaga's head!

00:04:06.170 --> 00:04:10.810
My lord, our campaign is doing 
even better than we expected.

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:15.250
I didn't think Asakura 
would surrender so quickly.

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:18.080
Stay vigilant, though.

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:22.380
I certainly will!

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:23.560
My lord!

00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:28.420
This is from Oichi-sama 
at Odani Castle.

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:29.790
From Oi-cchan?

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:33.920
What's this?

00:04:34.570 --> 00:04:37.160
It appears to contain red beans.

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:38.090
Red beans?

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:40.040
Why red beans?

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:41.550
I don't know.

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:45.410
I know what it means!

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:55.270
<i>What is this smell?</i>

00:04:55.720 --> 00:04:59.040
Too bad we don't have sugar.

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:01.850
Bean jam's gotta be sweet.

00:05:01.850 --> 00:05:05.040
Well, it's good salted, too.

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:10.090
Well, we're sweating a lot, 
so we should load up on salt.

00:05:10.090 --> 00:05:12.440
My lord, what exactly are you —

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:14.110
Hey, Micchi.

00:05:14.110 --> 00:05:16.510
Oi-cchan sent me red beans.

00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:19.250
I figured she wants us 
to eat up and be strong.

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:20.870
Oichi-sama did?

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:25.290
It's too small a thing 
for a mid-campaign gift.

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:31.110
My lord, was there nothing else? 
No letter?

00:05:31.110 --> 00:05:33.980
No, just red beans.

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:37.030
There was just one unusual thing.

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:43.940
Both sides of the bag were tied tightly.

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:45.440
Both sides?

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:49.690
Do you think she is implying 
something, Takenaka-dono?

00:05:52.110 --> 00:05:57.850
It could be serious if she 
is implying "bagged rat".

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:02.040
Bagged rat...

00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:04.590
What's that mean?

00:06:05.830 --> 00:06:09.510
It means Azai betrayed us.

00:06:11.630 --> 00:06:15.940
Indeed, if Azai were to 
attack us now from Oumi,

00:06:15.940 --> 00:06:19.580
we would be surrounded by Asakura
from the north and Azai from the south.

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:24.090
With no escape route, we would be 
trapped in enemy territory.

00:06:24.090 --> 00:06:26.750
That is, a bagged rat.

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:29.600
Of course, we cannot be sure.

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:32.510
Azai betraying us?

00:06:32.510 --> 00:06:33.720
Impossible!

00:06:35.320 --> 00:06:37.060
Bagged rat.

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:39.120
That's vague.

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:40.520
My lord!

00:06:41.720 --> 00:06:45.250
Azai's army is headed this way.

00:06:45.650 --> 00:06:49.930
Nagamasa Azai-dono seems 
to have betrayed us!

00:06:50.630 --> 00:06:52.630
But... no way.

00:06:52.630 --> 00:06:54.680
I cannot believe it!

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:59.070
Even these red beans, 
are they really from Oichi-sama?

00:06:59.070 --> 00:07:01.820
Yeah, they must be.

00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:03.940
It's got a snake pattern on it.

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:06.910
Who else would use something 
like this but Oi-cchan?

00:07:07.910 --> 00:07:11.360
My lord, what shall we do?

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:14.020
Ichijoudani is right there.

00:07:14.020 --> 00:07:16.190
It'll all be for nothing 
if we retreat now.

00:07:16.190 --> 00:07:19.010
Isn't there some way 
we can counterattack?

00:07:19.010 --> 00:07:20.110
There is not.

00:07:20.110 --> 00:07:21.830
Odani Castle is nearby.

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:24.350
We would not have time 
to move our army.

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:28.910
My lord, what are you doing?

00:07:28.910 --> 00:07:30.970
We'll be faster with less weight.

00:07:31.390 --> 00:07:32.940
We've lost this war!

00:07:33.510 --> 00:07:36.220
I'm bailing.

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:40.010
All forces, retreat!

00:07:40.010 --> 00:07:43.830
<i>This would come to be known as 
the Retreat at Kanegasaki.</i>

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:46.570
<i>It was the beginning of 
a retreating fight</i>

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:49.100
<i>that would be etched in the history 
of the Warring States.</i>

00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:52.890
My lord!

00:07:54.060 --> 00:07:55.610
What's up, Hideyoshi-kun?

00:07:55.610 --> 00:07:59.170
Would you allow me to command the rear?

00:07:59.170 --> 00:08:02.430
Oh. The rear. I forgot about that.

00:08:02.430 --> 00:08:04.630
If you command me,

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:09.000
I promise with my life to stop 
the Azai and Asakura armies.

00:08:09.370 --> 00:08:11.160
Hashiba-dono...

00:08:11.160 --> 00:08:14.080
To think he would volunteer 
himself for the rear guard.

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:18.990
It will be difficult for the rear guard
to come home in a situation like this.

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:20.390
Fine.

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:23.270
I'm leaving the rear guard to you.

00:08:23.650 --> 00:08:24.530
Yes, sir!

00:08:24.880 --> 00:08:26.240
Come back alive.

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:32.170
Yes, sir! 
Thank you for your kind words!

00:08:40.560 --> 00:08:42.970
Is it true that Azai betrayed us?

00:08:42.970 --> 00:08:45.400
Shibata-dono and Miwa-dono.

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:46.420
Where is the lord?

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:48.460
Has he left?

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:51.640
Yes. Upon hearing about Azai's betrayal,

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:54.480
he immediately declared 
a retreat, and ran back.

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:57.360
He is as embarrassingly 
quick as always.

00:08:57.360 --> 00:08:59.500
How many men did he take?

00:08:59.500 --> 00:09:02.240
Knowing him, he must not 
have taken many.

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:04.020
Five hundred? No, three hundred?

00:09:04.340 --> 00:09:05.390
Perhaps ten.

00:09:05.390 --> 00:09:07.680
I see, ten. Ten?!

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:10.320
That is dangerous, 
to go with so few.

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:14.660
I'm sure that a larger army would slow 
him down and make him more visible.

00:09:14.660 --> 00:09:18.440
He chose to be fast and 
to go in a small group.

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:20.620
We can only pray for him.

00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:25.200
In that case, we must also escape 
quickly from Kanegasaki too,

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:27.450
and think about heading to Kyoto.

00:09:27.450 --> 00:09:28.660
Yes.

00:09:28.660 --> 00:09:32.550
Let us all lead our men 
in an immediate retreat.

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:35.270
But what about the rear guard?

00:09:35.270 --> 00:09:37.900
I have the rear guard.

00:09:37.900 --> 00:09:41.600
I discussed it with the lord, 
and received his permission.

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:42.930
Is that so?

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:44.790
It will be a difficult battle.

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:45.930
Thank you.

00:09:45.930 --> 00:09:47.940
Leave it to me.

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:51.190
I pray for all of your fortunes.

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:53.560
Well, then. I'll be going.

00:09:56.190 --> 00:09:59.950
The rear guard is the most brutal.

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:02.600
He seems quite relaxed.

00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:08.170
He's faking it,
or he has confidence in his abilities.

00:10:09.370 --> 00:10:11.510
Hideyoshi Hashiba.

00:10:11.510 --> 00:10:13.800
That man is a mystery.

00:10:20.260 --> 00:10:23.260
<i>Nobunaga's situation right now</i>

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:26.750
<i>is just like Yoshimoto Imagawa's, 
way back when.</i>

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:31.840
<i>If I betray him at the 
rear guard, Oda is ruined.</i>

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:36.670
<i>Nobunaga, it's your turn to go down.</i>

00:10:36.670 --> 00:10:40.510
<i>It'll be just like the humiliation I felt 
when you defeated Yoshimoto.</i>

00:10:40.510 --> 00:10:43.080
<i>I'm going to avenge myself now!</i>

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:44.190
Hashiba-dono.

00:10:48.090 --> 00:10:50.030
I must speak with you.

00:10:52.870 --> 00:10:53.790
My lord!

00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:55.630
What is it?

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:58.060
The Oda army has 
learned of our plans!

00:10:58.060 --> 00:11:00.810
They're preparing to retreat now!

00:11:00.810 --> 00:11:01.640
What?

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:02.960
Retreating?

00:11:02.960 --> 00:11:04.410
Are they really?

00:11:04.410 --> 00:11:05.400
Yes.

00:11:06.410 --> 00:11:08.010
<i>So fast.</i>

00:11:08.010 --> 00:11:11.630
<i>How could they have decided 
to retreat so quickly?</i>

00:11:12.210 --> 00:11:17.030
<i>For Nobunaga, this should be the 
perfect opportunity to defeat Asakura.</i>

00:11:17.650 --> 00:11:20.400
<i>He is throwing all of that 
away to retreat.</i>

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:23.500
<i>No normal man could 
make such a decision.</i>

00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:24.420
My lord.

00:11:25.520 --> 00:11:26.650
We must hurry.

00:11:26.650 --> 00:11:29.640
It will take time to move our men.

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:32.870
I trust that we know 
where Nobunaga is.

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:38.340
Unfortunately, we could not find anyone 
that looks like Nobunaga in the main army.

00:11:38.690 --> 00:11:39.710
What?

00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:41.500
Nobunaga is...

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:44.990
...missing?

00:11:49.700 --> 00:11:50.680
Unforgivable!

00:11:51.290 --> 00:11:55.630
The lord truly believed in Asai-dono!

00:11:55.630 --> 00:11:56.770
I guess.

00:11:57.790 --> 00:12:00.110
I'm frustrated, too!

00:12:00.110 --> 00:12:03.950
Betray and be betrayed. Is this the way 
the Warring States world is?

00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:09.100
I'm sure our lord will have 
the last laugh.

00:12:13.950 --> 00:12:15.540
Fire!

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:20.600
Retreat!

00:12:20.600 --> 00:12:22.630
Don't let them get any closer!

00:12:23.210 --> 00:12:25.460
Don't fear the rifles!

00:12:25.460 --> 00:12:28.080
Take the heads of the mounted men!

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:33.740
Argh! This is becoming dangerous.

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:48.850
Takenaka's Mino army.

00:12:48.850 --> 00:12:50.810
They sure are strong.

00:12:50.810 --> 00:12:53.470
Rifles, bows, ready!

00:12:53.470 --> 00:12:54.660
Fire!

00:12:56.830 --> 00:12:57.980
Retreat!

00:12:58.400 --> 00:13:01.050
Keep distance with the enemy!

00:13:02.560 --> 00:13:06.740
<i>Dammit! I was supposed to betray Oda.</i>

00:13:06.740 --> 00:13:10.180
<i>Why am I desperately leading his rear guard?!</i>

00:13:10.180 --> 00:13:15.710
We would like to join you 
in the rear guard.

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:23.720
Specifically, we will take the second 
rear guard and protect you from behind.

00:13:23.720 --> 00:13:24.630
Do you agree?

00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:26.230
But, Akechi-dono...

00:13:26.230 --> 00:13:33.520
It may not be much, but I would like 
my Mino army to join your army.

00:13:34.210 --> 00:13:37.460
The more men the better, I expect.

00:13:39.560 --> 00:13:42.060
Wow! Thanks so much!

00:13:42.060 --> 00:13:45.460
Your kindness warms my heart.

00:13:47.110 --> 00:13:50.680
But I expect you both understand.

00:13:50.680 --> 00:13:54.180
The rear guard will have many casualties.

00:13:54.180 --> 00:13:58.000
There is no reason to create more.

00:13:58.580 --> 00:14:03.160
Akechi-dono, you are quite valuable 
to the Oda family.

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:09.670
Please trust my Hashiba army 
and leave it to us.

00:14:09.670 --> 00:14:16.320
Hashiba-dono, we are not offering 
to do this for your sake.

00:14:16.840 --> 00:14:24.000
We want to do everything we can 
for the Oda family, to protect the lord.

00:14:25.540 --> 00:14:26.920
I'm sure you feel

00:14:28.950 --> 00:14:31.430
exactly the same way.

00:14:34.610 --> 00:14:36.550
So let us fight together.

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:44.270
<i>Takenaka in the middle, 
Akechi in the back.</i>

00:14:44.270 --> 00:14:47.210
<i>I can't betray them like this!</i>

00:14:47.210 --> 00:14:51.950
<i>Argh! Have they figured me out?</i>

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:56.970
<i>If they have, they'll attack me the moment 
I do anything suspicious.</i>

00:14:56.970 --> 00:15:02.080
<i>My army will have nowhere to retreat, 
and we'll be annihilated.</i>

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:04.140
<i>The only way for me to survive</i>

00:15:04.140 --> 00:15:08.780
<i>is to fight like hell
and make this retreat successful!</i>

00:15:08.780 --> 00:15:11.080
Argh!

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:13.740
Fire!

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:17.880
What?

00:15:17.880 --> 00:15:19.660
Nobunaga is back?

00:15:19.660 --> 00:15:20.270
Yes.

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:23.470
I am told that he arrived 
at Kyoto last night.

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:27.330
But isn't that just wrong?

00:15:27.330 --> 00:15:28.690
It was just yesterday

00:15:28.690 --> 00:15:33.610
that I heard Nagamasa Azai betrayed him 
and was now trying to surround him.

00:15:33.610 --> 00:15:36.880
How can Nobunaga 
already be back? Huh?

00:15:36.880 --> 00:15:41.870
I believe he chose to retreat 
as soon as he heard of the betrayal.

00:15:50.940 --> 00:15:53.250
<i>I'm really tired...</i>

00:15:53.250 --> 00:15:54.810
Hey!

00:15:55.350 --> 00:15:57.220
Welcome back!

00:15:57.220 --> 00:15:59.390
Thank you!

00:16:03.820 --> 00:16:06.240
Great job back there, Hideyoshi-kun!

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:08.760
I thank you for your kind words!

00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:10.510
I'm glad you made it back.

00:16:10.510 --> 00:16:11.790
Yes, sir.

00:16:11.790 --> 00:16:13.520
What did you think?

00:16:13.520 --> 00:16:18.520
I did not notice any 
suspicious actions.

00:16:18.520 --> 00:16:21.960
He appeared to be fighting at 
the rear guard very hard.

00:16:22.990 --> 00:16:28.270
Have we been paranoid in 
thinking he was dangerous?

00:16:28.270 --> 00:16:29.050
Perhaps.

00:16:29.690 --> 00:16:34.010
His true intentions are 
still difficult to know.

00:16:38.270 --> 00:16:41.850
I can just picture Nobunaga's panic.

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:44.190
Nobunaga's demise is certain.

00:16:44.190 --> 00:16:47.930
Yes, this is a complete 
victory for us.

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:56.740
What are you celebrating for?

00:16:57.720 --> 00:17:00.800
Do you men not understand 
how grave it is

00:17:00.800 --> 00:17:02.950
that we have not taken his head?

00:17:03.570 --> 00:17:07.670
The sole purpose of this war 
was to take Nobunaga's head.

00:17:08.110 --> 00:17:13.050
Taking the heads of a few thousand
foot soldiers accomplishes nothing!

00:17:14.150 --> 00:17:15.310
Father.

00:17:16.860 --> 00:17:18.720
Everyone knows that.

00:17:19.570 --> 00:17:20.760
But for now,

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:24.890
please let them enjoy themselves.

00:17:24.890 --> 00:17:30.200
<b>Conquest By Force of Arms</b>

00:17:31.050 --> 00:17:33.690
My lord! Let us quickly 
subjugate South Oumi,

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:36.400
and begin our attack on Azai!

00:17:36.400 --> 00:17:40.280
Neglecting a betrayer 
will only create more betrayal.

00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:44.540
My lord, your opinion?

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:49.150
You know, I thought the closer 
you got to conquering Japan,

00:17:49.150 --> 00:17:52.530
the fewer enemies there'd be.

00:17:52.530 --> 00:17:54.920
I guess that's not how it works.

00:17:55.400 --> 00:17:57.940
In fact, it's just the opposite.

00:17:57.940 --> 00:18:01.640
We might never finish it 
at this rate.

00:18:01.640 --> 00:18:02.510
My lord!

00:18:03.280 --> 00:18:04.190
Yes?

00:18:04.190 --> 00:18:07.270
I cannot accept you saying that!

00:18:07.270 --> 00:18:12.000
Have you not always said to us,
 full of confidence,

00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:14.530
that you would conquer Japan?

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:16.240
Yes, my lord!

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:19.690
We've followed you because of 
your unwavering confidence,

00:18:19.690 --> 00:18:21.970
and the success you've had to justify it!

00:18:21.970 --> 00:18:26.410
It is unlike you to whine.

00:18:26.800 --> 00:18:28.870
...What?

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:31.300
I didn't think I was whining.

00:18:31.300 --> 00:18:33.310
I was just making an observation.

00:18:33.310 --> 00:18:34.280
My lord!

00:18:35.850 --> 00:18:38.810
We cannot turn back now.

00:18:39.740 --> 00:18:42.880
If we stop now, the Oda family 
will be destroyed.

00:18:43.440 --> 00:18:45.180
We cannot stop.

00:18:45.690 --> 00:18:47.330
We must keep running.

00:18:48.080 --> 00:18:50.220
Otherwise, we will not conquer Japan!

00:18:53.380 --> 00:18:54.740
I know.

00:18:55.460 --> 00:18:57.490
I don't intend to stop.

00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:01.160
We'll fight Azai, and win.

00:19:01.680 --> 00:19:05.540
I have to conquer Japan, after all.

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:13.800
My lord!

00:19:14.240 --> 00:19:15.310
Yeah?

00:19:15.820 --> 00:19:21.430
Of course we are fighting Azai,
but one thing bothers me.

00:19:22.950 --> 00:19:24.480
About Oi-cchan?

00:19:30.880 --> 00:19:32.060
Oichi.

00:19:33.040 --> 00:19:36.200
You've been saying 
ever since we married

00:19:36.980 --> 00:19:39.740
that your brother 
was more interesting than me.

00:19:41.310 --> 00:19:45.880
Having him as my enemy,
I finally understand what you meant.

00:19:47.930 --> 00:19:50.090
He truly is.

00:19:50.090 --> 00:19:52.850
Nobunaga is an interesting man.

00:19:56.400 --> 00:20:00.370
Your brother apparently fled the 
battleground by himself.

00:20:01.100 --> 00:20:04.000
He left behind his retainers 
and his men.

00:20:04.900 --> 00:20:11.860
He bet on the speed of a small group 
over the strength of a large army.

00:20:13.170 --> 00:20:17.460
And Nobunaga won the bet,
 and survived.

00:20:19.280 --> 00:20:20.490
Oichi.

00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:25.800
Your brother must be quite lucky.

00:20:29.130 --> 00:20:31.020
You cannot defeat my brother.

00:20:34.420 --> 00:20:37.580
You cannot defeat my brother.

00:20:38.570 --> 00:20:40.000
Don't be so sure.

00:20:40.000 --> 00:20:42.320
We already won this battle.

00:20:44.340 --> 00:20:47.220
But my brother is alive.

00:20:48.080 --> 00:20:51.050
True, it hurts that we 
could not kill Nobunaga.

00:20:51.610 --> 00:20:54.810
But this is just the beginning.

00:20:57.940 --> 00:20:59.690
This is just the beginning.

00:20:59.690 --> 00:21:01.300
Nagamasa-dono.

00:21:03.170 --> 00:21:08.430
Oichi, I received a letter from Nobunaga 
asking for your return.

00:21:10.670 --> 00:21:12.770
I'm not going back.

00:21:16.590 --> 00:21:20.030
I'll stay here, and persuade you!
